  "summaries": [
    {
      "id": 15120,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "One of our package servers had an old smtpd service linked with openssl 1.0.1i, which uses nondeterministic CBC padding, making it easy for man-in-the-middle attackers to obtain cleartext data via a padding-oracle attack, aka the \"POODLE\" issue. The service has been disabled for the internet, as it was not necessary to begin with.",
